# The working copy lives on a Windows drive under WSL, where an editor can
# rewrite a tracked text file with CRLF endings. Git keeps LF in the object
# store, so every rewritten file then reads as modified while its content is
# unchanged. `text=auto` makes git detect text, store and check out LF, and
# convert a CRLF working file back to LF when it reads it. `git status` stays
# clean even after a Windows tool touches the file.
#
# `text=auto` also detects a binary file and leaves its bytes alone. This
# repository tracks no binary file today; a future one needs no rule here.
* text=auto eol=lf
